The fixtures of the mise package's linked test
(packages/mise/MiseTest/Linked/Mise/Contract.lean, miseContractChecks and
the checks beside it), which the linked test reads from this directory, the
package's tests/process-environment, and copies into each check's own
temporary directory. Both must stay executable (mode 100755).

- mise: stands for mise. `mise env --json` prints a JSON object whose PATH
  is the line in the file fixture-path of the directory it runs in, so two
  directories get two PATHs. In a directory that holds the file
  fixture-fail it prints `mise fixture: failing here` on its standard
  error and exits 1.
- slow-mise: stands for a mise that outlives the lookup's time limit. It
  sleeps for 30 seconds, and is killed first.
